1453	 ## Limitations
1454	 
1455	 Request translation drops the following content (some drops log a `tracing` warning):
1456	 
1457	 - **Remote-URL images** — only inline base64-encoded images are forwarded; `ContentPart::ImageUrl` variants with remote URLs are omitted.
1458	 - **Audio parts** — audio `ContentPart` variants are not supported by this provider and are dropped.
1459	 - **Non-text tool-result parts** — only the text content of tool results is forwarded; image or structured-data parts in tool results are omitted.
1460	 - **Duplicate tool results and empty text** — a second tool result for one call is dropped, with a `tracing` warning on target `paigasus::gemini::translate`. Empty text parts are dropped too.
1461	 
1462	+Tool loops on Gemini 3 work. The provider keeps each `thoughtSignature` as `ContentPart::ProviderData` (key `PROVIDER_DATA_KEY`, value `"gemini"`) and sends it back on its own call. It restores the call order that Gemini returned. For a call of the current turn that has no valid signature, it sends the documented dummy value `skip_thought_signature_validator`. A signature from another model id or another API counts as not valid. These limits apply:
1463	+
1464	+- **Vertex** — Vertex signatures are not live-tested.
1465	+- **Dummy value** — it is live-tested only on `gemini-3.8-flash` (Developer API). It is not tested on Gemini 2.x (these ids return 404 for new users) or on Vertex.
1466	+- **Text-level signatures** — they are not sent back.
1467	+
1468	 The following feature is not yet implemented:
1469	 
1470	 - **Reasoning streaming** — Gemini's `thoughtsContent` field in streaming responses is currently discarded. Reasoning delta events (`ModelEvent::ReasoningDelta`) are not emitted by this provider. This will be addressed in a future release.
1471	 
